    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** (67.77) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.00) anchor the offense as our clear top-tier options. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a steady projection profile that holds firm even against Brandon Sproat, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a favorable park adjustment and strong underlying xwOBA, despite a minor platoon tax. **Gunnar Henderson** (63.80) remains a high-upside play; while he faces the typically stingy Framber Valdez, the ballpark dynamics and his high sprint speed\u2014compounded by the opportunity to exploit Valdez\u2019s slow delivery for stolen bases\u2014make him an essential component of our efficiency-focused strategy. **Coby Mayo** (60.33) also warrants a start; he leverages the same park-induced offensive boost as **Gunnar Henderson**, and his ability to handle left-handed pitching provides a necessary balance to the bottom of our lineup.\n\nThe bench decision regarding **Nolan Schanuel** (49.36) was the most difficult to resolve. While he projected better than **Dominic Smith** (41.03), the optimizer opted for **Dominic Smith** to manage positional flexibility and game caps in anticipation of late-breaking lineup changes, effectively keeping **Nolan Schanuel** on ice as a premium contingency. We are keeping a close watch on **Sam Antonacci** (53.52) and **Miguel Vargas** (57.48), both of whom are projected based on assumed lineup spots. While the wind-out conditions at their respective venues provide a solid floor for their power-hitting potential, they are high-variance starts that require official confirmation of the batting order to fully validate their high scores. \n\nRegarding risks, we are proceeding with caution regarding our reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Nasim Nunez**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Sam Antonacci**. While their efficiency scores are competitive, the lack of confirmed spots means any unexpected drop in the batting order\u2014or a late scratch\u2014could shift these marginal plays below our acceptable threshold. **Liam Hicks** (51.54) faces the sternest test of the day against Christian Scott; while the platoon advantage is favorable, his score is lower than preferred, making him our most volatile starter in the C1 slot. With **Jorge Polanco** confirmed out on the IL, we are focused on protecting our remaining daily game caps while hunting for steals via **Gunnar Henderson** and the high-speed options throughout the depth chart.",
